        "titulo": "The typical English-speaker mistakes",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: the costliest mistakes: using wo for everything, because English \"where\" covers all three (a destination needs wohin, an origin woher); keeping the subject before the verb in a question (Wo du wohnst? instead of Wo wohnst du?); looking for a \"do\" that German doesn't have; and mixing up wer (\"who\") with \"where\". STEP 2: read the table and say each correct sentence out loud before you look at the reason.",
